From: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] can: gs_usb: support up to 4 CAN interfaces

The RDK X5 ships a USB-to-CAN adapter that exposes four CAN channels. The
mainline driver caps the number of interfaces per device at three, so the
fourth channel is rejected during probe:

    gs_usb 1-1:1.0: Driver cannot handle more that 3 CAN interfaces

Raise GS_MAX_INTF to four. This mirrors the vendor SDK change carried as
roboparty_rdk/build_params/gs_usb.patch so the same adapter works on the
Armbian port.

Signed-off-by: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c b/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c
index 264a0f7..fd929ef 100644
--- a/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c
@@ -278,9 +278,9 @@ struct gs_host_frame {
 /* Only launch a max of GS_MAX_RX_URBS usb requests at a time. */
 #define GS_MAX_RX_URBS 30
 /* Maximum number of interfaces the driver supports per device.
- * Current hardware only supports 3 interfaces. The future may vary.
+ * Current hardware only supports 4 interfaces. The future may vary.
  */
-#define GS_MAX_INTF 3
+#define GS_MAX_INTF 4
 
 struct gs_tx_context {
 	struct gs_can *dev;
-- 
2.43.0
